<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anti-Comintern Pact</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1936">1936</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Agreement against the Communist International</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Anti-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/communist-international">Comintern</a> Pact was an anti-communist agreement concluded between Nazi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/empire-of-japan">Empire of Japan</a> on 25 November 1936, directed against the Communist International. It was signed by Joachim von Ribbentrop and the Japanese ambassador Kintomo Mushanokōji, and a secret additional protocol set a joint policy against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> joined in 1937, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> in 1939. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> distanced itself from Germany after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/molotov-ribbentrop-pact">Molotov–Ribbentrop Pact</a> of August 1939, and the pact was followed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tripartite-pact">Tripartite Pact</a> of September 1940. It was renewed in November 1941 with new members and ceased to exist with the end of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">World War II</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anti-comintern-pact.jpg" alt="Anti-Comintern Pact" width="330" height="211" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown photographer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anti-Comintern_Pact_signing_1936.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
